WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:06.620
After seven outings as Natasha Romanoff, Scarlett
Johansson is finally taking the lead in 2020's

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:07.380
Black Widow.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.910
But what does Marvel Studios have in store
for the master assassin?

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.380
How, exactly, is Johansson leading a new Marvel
movie when her character perished in Avengers:

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:16.880
Endgame?

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.140
Here's what we know.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:25.040
At the 2019 San Diego Comic-Con, Marvel Studios'
Kevin Feige unveiled the closely-guarded details

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:29.859
of the Marvel Cinematic Universe's "Phase
4," including official release dates for all

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:34.820
of the company's upcoming film and television
projects in 2020 and 2021.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:39.180
This announcement included a May 1st, 2020
release date for Black Widow, which shows

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.260
the company's faith in the character.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:45.940
May is the first month of Hollywood's traditional
"Summer Blockbuster" season, where movies

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:47.720
go to rake in the big bucks.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:52.059
It is obvious that opposing studios are trying
to steer clear of the Marvel money-making

00:00:52.059 --> 00:00:56.780
machine, with the release calendar surrounding
Black Widow being pretty sparse, outside of

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:01.500
counter-programming choices like Trolls: World
Tour and the third film in Reese Witherspoon's

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.220
Legally Blonde film series.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:09.720
Continuing their trend of making interesting
and unexpected directorial choices, Marvel

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:12.520
Studios has brought on Cate Shortland to direct
Black Widow.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.680
Shortland won the gig after a search that
had the comic book giant meeting with over

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.280
70 potential directors.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:23.040
According to The Hollywood Reporter, the search
lasted over half a year and finding a female

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.300
filmmaker was priority number one.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:29.980
Shortland eventually booked the highly-sought-after
job over other celebrated finalists.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:34.560
One factor that surely worked in Shortland's
favor was having Johansson in her corner,

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:37.700
as the actress apparently pushed Marvel to
hire the director.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:43.680
Johansson is reportedly a fan of Shortland's
female-led 2012 drama Lore, a critically acclaimed,

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:47.570
award-winning picture that tells the story
of a young woman who leads her siblings through

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:50.500
Germany in the immediate aftermath of World
War II.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:55.180
Shortland sounds like the ideal candidate
to show audiences everywhere exactly how much

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.490
red Romanoff's got in her ledger.

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:01.940
"I've got red in my ledger — I'd like to
wipe it out."

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:06.680
It should come as no surprise that Marvel
Studios is keeping Black Widow plot details

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:10.860
hush-hush at the moment, as that tends to
be their general modus operandi.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:15.020
Of the few details that members of the cast
and crew have let loose, it is interesting

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:19.570
that the film is set after Captain America:
Civil War and before the cataclysmic events

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:20.980
of Avengers: Infinity War.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:25.150
Marvel seems to be taking a more grounded
approach to their latest picture, which makes

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:29.840
sense following the outrageous bombast of
the last two Avengers movies and the globe-trotting

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.960
adventures of Spider-Man: Far from Home.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:37.280
After seeing the footage Marvel Studios screened
during the 2019 San Diego Comic-Con, Screen

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:42.140
Rant's Molly Freeman mentioned the company,
quote, "previewed a more grounded MCU movie,

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:47.120
one rooted in practical fights and a deeper
dive into Natasha's world of espionage."

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:51.531
Given the vast variety of different comic
books Marvel releases on a yearly basis, it

00:02:51.531 --> 00:02:55.940
is refreshing to see their big screen counterpart
begin to bring different styles of superhero

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:57.500
storytelling to the theater.

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:02.520
To the delight of Marvel fans everywhere,
Scarlett Johansson has signed on to return

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:06.300
as Black Widow and garnered a significant
pay increase to do so.

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:10.320
According to The Hollywood Reporter, Johansson
will finally be making an amount of money

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:15.590
that is equal to her male counterparts she
will be paid $15 million to appear in Black

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:20.250
Widow, the same amount Chris Evans and Chris
Hemsworth each earned for playing Captain

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:22.540
America and Thor in Avengers: Infinity War.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:27.340
For her part, Johnasson is excited to be returning
to the role for which she has become most

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:27.840
famous.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:31.580
Playing the Widow this time around should
provide the actress with more opportunity

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:36.150
than ever to dive deep into the character
as a lead rather than a supporting part.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.940
Johansson told Entertainment Weekly:

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:41.420
"Where we find Natasha in her life at this
point is very specific.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:45.780
She really is in a dark place where she's
got no one to call and nowhere to go.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.660
She's really grappling with her own self."

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:52.700
"Sir, I'm afraid no alcohol is allowed off
the premises."

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:55.780
"I can do anything I want…

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:57.940
I'm the chief of police."

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:03.100
Having hit a new level of nationwide recognition
due to starring in Netflix's retro phenomenon

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:07.920
Stranger Things, experienced character actor
David Harbour has been using that exposure

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:12.850
to book bigger gigs in Hollywood including,
of course, his upcoming role as the Red Guardian

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:13.760
in Black Widow.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:21.120
Introduced way back in 1967's Avengers #43,
Alexei Shostakov a.k.a. the Red Guardian was

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:25.570
an acclaimed test pilot whose heroism caught
the attention of the Russian authorities who

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:30.410
wanted a national hero to represent them,
just as Captain America represented the United

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:30.980
States.

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:35.120
Harbour is excited for his chance to play
a Russian take on the Captain America-esque

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:35.660
soldier.

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:36.860
He told EW:

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:41.080
"In a way he's a super-soldier, but he's also
a very complicated guy.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:44.360
He has a lot of flaws, a lot of idiosyncrasies.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.900
It's a very rich character."

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:51.480
If you are not an avid reader of Marvel Comics,
you might be surprised to learn that Natasha

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:53.240
Romanoff is not the only Black Widow.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:57.900
Another character who has used the moniker
is Yelena Belova, initially created as an

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.800
antagonist for Romanoff in the late 1990s.

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:05.100
Florence Pugh will be starring in Black Widow
as Belova, though it is unknown if she will

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:08.480
be a protagonist, antagonist, or something
in-between.

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:13.170
Pugh has turned heads in recent years, having
turned in an award-winning performance in

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:18.070
2016's Lady Macbeth as well as starring in
the critically-acclaimed 2019 horror film

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:18.660
Midsommar.

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:23.440
The actress describes Belova as Natasha's,
quote, "sister figure" and has teased fans

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:24.160
by saying:

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:27.150
"They meet one another and it's quite heightened
and heated."

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:33.090
As the 2020 release date for Black Widow creeps
closer and closer, more details keep leaking

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:35.940
out on the next chapter in the Marvel Cinematic
Universe.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:40.240
Outside of Johansson, Rachel Weisz is the
biggest Hollywood name set to appear in Black

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:40.740
Widow.

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:45.140
The English actress is a true movie star,
having appeared in everything from blockbusters

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:51.280
like 1999's The Mummy and 2012's The Bourne
Legacy to awards fare like 2005's The Constant

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.500
Gardener and 2018's The Favourite.

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:58.050
She'll star as yet another Black Widow named
Melina, an original character for the film

00:05:58.050 --> 00:06:01.500
who is apparently just one of numerous women
to wear that mantle.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:06.920
The Handmaid's Tale's O-T Fagbenle has been
cast as Mason, an ally from Romanoff's S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:11.320
days who is romantically interested in her,
while prolific English actor Ray Winstone

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:13.680
has been cast in an undisclosed role.

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:17.440
Even though there has not been an official
casting announcement nor confirmation that

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:21.889
the character is in the film, based on the
footage shown at the 2019 San Diego Comic-Con,

00:06:21.889 --> 00:06:26.510
it appears that classic Marvel Comics villain
Taskmaster will have a part to play in all

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:27.510
of the mayhem.

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:32.610
A supervillain with genius-level intellect,
Taskmaster continues the "trust no one" theme

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:35.060
that Marvel seems to be going for with Black
Widow.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:39.260
There have been times through his publication
history in Marvel Comics where Taskmaster

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:44.140
has proven to be an anti-hero, working with
superheroes against the evil powers that be.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:49.880
Only time will tell what role he plays in
Natasha Romanoff's next and likely final big-screen

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:50.480
outing.

